    "ls|LS17_S6_U_1": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*1 \nANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n \nIMPACT OF COVID-19 PANDEMIC ON INDIAN TOURISM INDUSTRY \n \n†*1. SHRI RAMESH CHANDER KAUSHIK:  \nSHRI RAJU BISTA:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has constituted any working group to \nassess the impact of Covid -19 pandemic on tourism industry \nand if so, the details thereof along with the quantum of loss in \nterms of job losses and foreign exchange loss, State/UT-wise;  \n(b)  the number of foreign tourists visited the country during first \nand second waves of Covid-19;  \n(c)  whether the Government has received proposals from various \nStates including Haryana, North -Eastern States, West Bengal, \nOdisha, Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu for new projects for \ncomprehensive development/rejuvenation of tourism sector, \nallocation of more funds, giving moratorium to loans availed by \ntourism industry after the pandemic, etc., if so, the details \nthereof and the action taken thereon;  \n(d)  whether the Government has set up/plans to set up a Vaccine \nCertification Programme for foreign tourists; and  \n(e)  the details of hot els/homestays/tourist services/ organizations \nregistered with the Ministry in various States including \nDarjeeling and Kalimpong districts? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF TOURISM            (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n  \n*********** \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  †*1 ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \nREGARDING IMPACT OF COVID -19 PANDEMIC ON INDIAN TOURISM \nINDUSTRY \n \n(a):  Ministry of Tourism has constituted a Task Force with Hon’ble \nMinister for Tourism in chair and State Tourism Ministers, Joint \nSecretary level officers of concerned Central Ministries and \nrepresentatives from industry associations, to meet the challenge \nposed by the outbreak of COVID 19 and make appropriate \nrecommendations for the revival of the tourism and hospitality \nsector in the country.  \n \nMinistry of Tourism engaged the National Council  of Applied \nEconomic Research (NCAER) in January, 2021 to conduct study on \n‘India and the Corona Virus Pandemic: Economic Losses for \nHouseholds Engaged in Tourism and Policies for Recovery’.  The \nstudy observes that a significant number of jobs were lost in  the \ntourism sector once the lockdown was implemented. 14.5 million \njobs during Q1,5.2 million jobs during Q2 and 1.8 million jobs during \nQ3 are expected to have been lost as compared to an estimated \n34.8 million jobs in the pre pandemic period of 2019-20 (direct jobs). \n \nThe percentage change in Foreign Exchange Earnings (FEE) \nduring the months January to December 2020 as compared to the \ncorresponding period in 2019 is -76.3%.  \n \nThe Ministry has not conducted any formal study to assess the \nState/UT-wise impact of Covid 19 pandemic on tourism industry. \n \n(b): The details of Foreign Tourist Arrivals during 2020 and 2021 \nare at Annexure I. \n \n(c): Details of project proposals approved for grant of Central \nFinancial Assistance under the National Mission on Pilgrima ge \nRejuvenation and Spiritual, Heritage Augmentation Drive \n(PRASHAD) and Assistance to Central Agencies for Infrastructure \nDevelopment Schemes are at Annexure II.   \n \nStates/UTs have requested for sympathetic consideration for \ngiving moratorium on loans etc ., which has been taken up with the \nMinistry of Finance.  \n\n \n(d): The Government of India has not yet announced a Vaccine \nCertification Programme for foreign tourists. \n \n(e): The details of hotels / homestays registered with the Ministry in \nvarious states are  placed at Annexure III . The details of  tourist \nservices / organisations (Travel Trade Service Providers) in various \nstates are at Annexure IV. \n \nThe details of Hotels/ Homestays/tourist services/organizations \nregistered with Ministry of Tourism under the N ational Integrated \nDatabase of Hospitality Industry (NIDHI) Scheme at Darjeeling and \nKalimpong are mentioned in the following table: \n \nSl. \nNo. \nDistrict Hotels/ Homestays Tourist services/ \norganizations (Tour \nOperator) \n1 Darjeeling 6 1 \n2 Kalimpong 7 -- \n \n*********** \n\n             ANNEXURE- I \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (b) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. †*1 ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 REGARDING IMPACT \nOF COVID-19 PANDEMIC ON INDIAN TOURISM INDUSTRY \n \nForeign Tourist Arrivals (FTAs) during 2020 and 2021: \nS. \nNo. \nMonth FTAs during 2020 FTAs during 2021 \n(P) \n1. January 11,19,250 83,822 \n2. February 10,18,440 99,640 \n3. March 3,28,304 1,23,179 \n4. April 2,820 69,442 \n5. May 3,764 13,307 \n6. June 8,590 - \n7. July 12,655 - \n8. August 19,761 - \n9. September 28,167 - \n10. October 41,494 - \n11. November 70,977 - \n12. December 90,544 - \n \nSource: Bureau of Immigration \nP: Provisional \n \n********** \n\nANNEXURE – II \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. \n†*1 ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 REGARDING IMPACT OF COVI D-19 PANDEMIC \nON INDIAN TOURISM INDUSTRY \n  \nApproved Projects under PRASHAD Scheme \n(Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState Name of the Project Project \nCost \nAmount \nReleased \n Year 2020-21    \n1 Meghalaya Development of Pilgrimage \nFacilitation in Meghalaya  \n29.32 6.53 \n2 Chhattisgarh Development of Maa Bamleshwari \nDevi Temple, Rajnandgaon, \nDongargarh, Chhattisgarh \n43.33 12.16 \n3 Arunachal \nPradesh \nDevelopment of Parasuram Kund, \nLohit  \n37.88 Adm. Sac. \n5.1.21 \n4 Madhya Pradesh Development of Amarkantak, \nMadhya Pradesh \n49.99 08.01.2021 \n5 Sikkim Development of Pilgrimage \nFacilitation at Four Patron Saints, \nYuksom, Sikkim \n33.32 9.50 \n6 Telangana Development of Jogulamba Devi \nTemple, Alampur, Telangana \n36.73 5.14 \n7 Tripura Development of Tripura Sundari \nTemple, Udaipur, Tripura \n37.8