    "ls|LS17_S6_U_125": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK  SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.125 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28.07.2021 \n \nRAILWAY NETWORK IN GUJARAT  \n \n†*125.  SHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM:    \n \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:   \n \n(a) whether  several areas in Gujarat are still not connected by railway \nnetwork due to which people in the said areas are deprived of railway \nfacility and development in these areas is stalled; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c) the time by which the Government proposes to start projects to connect \nthese areas of Gujarat by railway network to ensure railway facility for \npeople living in the said areas and also development of these areas? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****    \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 125 BY SHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA  ON 28.07.2021 REGARDING RAILWAY \nNETWORK IN GUJARAT  \n \n(a) to (c): Gujarat State is very well connected with Railway Network. As on \n01.04.2020, total 5301 route km of railway track exists in Gujarat.  \n \n To further improve the railway connectivity, 4 new line railway \nprojects of total length 479 km costing `5,006 crore, are in different stages \nof planning/sanction/executio n, falling fully/partly in the S tate of Gujarat. \nOut of above, 79 km length has been commissioned and an expenditure of \n`1772 crore has b een incurred upto March, 2021. These projects will \nprovide connectivity to deprived areas. \n \n Major ports of Gujarat namely Kandla, Mundra, Porbander, Pipavav, \nDahej are already well connected with Railway Network.  To boost further \ndevelopment, existing railway tracks are also being doubled.  At present, \n11 doubling projects covering a length of 1612 km at a cost of `15,163 \ncrore are in different stages of Planning/S anction/Execution, falling \nfully/partly in the State of Gujarat. Out of above, 272 km double line has \nbeen commissioned and an expenditure of `3,717 crore has been incurred \nupto March, 2021. \n  \n Average Annual Budget allocation for infrastructure projects a nd \nsafety works, falling fully/partly in the State of Gujarat, during 2014 -19 has \nincreased to `3327 crore per year, from `589 crore per year (during 2009 -\n14). Thus the average annual budget allocation during 2014 -19 is 465% \nmore than average annual budget  allocation of 2009 -14 ( `589 crore per \nyear). Total Budget outlay for these works for financial year 2021 -22 is \n`4,484 crore, which is 661% more than average annual budget outlay of \n2009-14.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_126": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 126 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28.07.2021 \n \nUPGRADATION OF CALICUT RAILWAY STATION \n \n*126. SHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government plans to upgrade Calicut railway \nstation with the help of Indian Railway  Stations Development \nCorporation (IRSDC); \n (b) if so, the details regarding the plans proposed in this regard; \n(c) whether any progress has been made  by IRSDC  in the \ndevelopment of Calicut railway station to international \nstandards; and \n(d) if so, the details regarding the works undertaken in this \nregard? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n (a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n*****  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  126 BY SHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 28.07.2021 REGARDING \nUPGRADATION OF CALICUT RAILWAY STATION \n \n(a) to (d): Yes, Sir. Calicut (Kozhikode) railway station has been \nidentified for redevelopment and entrusted to Rail Land \nDevelopment Authority (RLDA) for redevelopment. RLDA has \nengaged consultant for carrying out  techno -economic studies i.e., \nfor Feasibility Studies, Detailed Master Planning, Urban Planning, \nEngineering and preparation of Detailed Project Report for \nredevelopment of the station under Public Private Partnership \nmodel. \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_127": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COAL  \nLOK   SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 127 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 28.07.2021  \n  \nUtilization of CSR Funds   \n  \n*127.  SHRI SANJAY SETH: \n  \n  \nWill the Minister of COAL be pleased to state: \n  \n(a)  whether the Government has formulated any scheme to utilize Corporate Social \nResponsibility (CSR) fund of coal companies for the development of coalfields especially in \nJharkhand; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with the details of such development works being carried out;  \n(c )       the quantum of funds accrued and utilized by coal PSUs for the purpose during the last \nthree years and the current year; \n(d)       the status of physical progress of such development works/activities;  \n(e)        whether any of the coal PSUs has defaulted in spending CSR funds and if so, the details \nthereof along with the corrective action taken by the Government thereon; and \n(f)        whether any relief is being provided to the families of the miners who suffered accidents \nand if so, the details thereof? \n  \n      \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF  PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS, COAL AND MINES \n (SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n  \n(a) to (f): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n  \n\n  \n  \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 127 FOR ANSWER \nON 28/7/2021 ASKED BY SHRI SANJAY SETH, M.P. REGARDING UTILIZATION OF \nCSR FUND.    \n  \n(a) & (b) :  Development works/activities are undertaken by Coal India Limited (CIL) and its \nsubsidiaries under Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR).  As per CSR policy of CIL, subsidiary \ncompanies undertake CSR works in their State(s) of operation and CIL undertakes  CSR works in \nwhole of India including the States covered by subsidiaries. Accordingly, Eastern Coalfields Ltd. \n(ECL), Bharat Coking Coal Ltd. (BCCL), Central Coalfields Ltd. (CCL) and Coal India Ltd. \n(CIL) have executed CSR works in the state of Jharkhand . The details of major CSR works in \nJharkhand during the last three years and current year are enclosed as Annexure A. \n  \n         \n(c) & (d):  The details of total CSR funds allocated by CIL subsidiaries operating in the State of \nJharkhand and the actual ex penditure in the State during the last three years and current year are \ngiven in the table below: \nFinancial Year Total CSR Statutory requirement \nas per Companies Act, 2013 of \nECL, BCCL, CCL \n(Rs. crores) \nActual CSR Expenditure \nin the state of Jharkhand \n(Rs. crores) \n2018-19 52.62 50.97 \n2019-20 58.97 65.81 \n2020-21 55.30 71.33 \n2021-22 (Provisional) 57.58  18.07 \n(Apr. – June 2021) \n(Provisional) \nThe physical progress of major CSR works in Jharkhand is attached as  in Annexure A. \n  \n(e):  No shortfall has been witnessed in utilization of   CSR funds in each of the last three years \ni.e. FY 18-19 to FY 20-21 in CIL and its subsidiaries collectively.   \n(f):   Although not a part of CSR, the following compensation is being provided uniformly in \nCoal India Limited and its subsidiaries: \n(A) Following compensation are being provided to the employee who suffered accidents or die \ndue to mine accident: \n1. Compensation under The Employee’s Compensation Act, 1923. \n2. An amount of  ₹ 15 lakh is paid as ex-gratia, in case of fatal mine accident. \n3. An amount upto ₹ 1,25,000/- is paid under the Life Cover Scheme in case of death. \n4. In addition to compensation under the Employee Compensation Act, an additional \namount of ₹ 90,000 is paid in case of death or permanent total disablement resulting on \n\naccount of accident arising out of and in course of employment is paid to non-executive \nemployees. \n5. Upto ₹ 20 Lakhs as per Payment of Gratuity (Amendment) Act, 2018. \n6. All employees are covered under the Coal Mines Provident Fund scheme with equal \nshares both by employees and the company. The accumulated amount is paid. \n7. Payment of leave encashment and any other dues. \n8. Pension as per Coal Mines Pension Scheme, 1998. \n9. Compassionate Employment is provided to one dependent of the deceased employee. In \nlieu of compassionate employment, monthly monetary compensation is paid to the female \ndependent of the deceased employee. This amount is revised with every wage revision. \nPresently the Monthly Monetary compensation is paid at ₹ 26,292.97& ₹ 40,000 per \nmonth for non-executives and executives respectively \n  \n (B) Relief/compensation to the families of Contract ors' workers who suffered accidents or die \ndue to mine accident: - \n1. Compensation under the Employee's compensation Act, 1923 \n2. An amount of  ₹ 15 lakh is paid to the next of kin of the contractors’ worker in case of \nfatal mine accident by the contractor. \n3. Amount of gratuity (if eligible) as per Payment of Gratuity (Amendment) Act, 2018 by \nthe contractor. \n4. Nominee of deceased contractors’ workers are eligible for payment of accumulated \namount under EPF/CMPF. \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \nAnnexure-A \nMajor CSR works in Jharkhand during 2018-19 to 2020-21 and the current year  \nS. \nNo. Subsidiary Year Project Details \nCSR \nFund \nSpent \n(Rs. Cr.) \nPhysical \nProgress \n1 CIL 2021-22 \nImprovement of Infrastructure at District \nHospital, Simdega  to tackle COVID -19 related \nchallenges \n0.99 Ongoing \n2 CIL 2021-22 Setting up oxygen generation plant at East \nSinghbhum, Jharkhand 0.65 Ongoing \n3 CIL 2021-22 Procurement of one Advance Life Support \n(ALS) ambulance for Palamu district 0.60 Ongoing \n4 ECL 2021-22 \nSetting up 200 bedded Dedicated COVID \nHospital (DCH) at newly constructed Hospital \nBuilding at Hansdiha in Saraiyahat Block of \nDumka District \n3.45 Ongoing \n5 ECL 2021-22 \nFund to Aspirational District Godda  for \nprocurement of medical and other equipments \nrequired to fight against COVID-19 \n3.40 Ongoing \n6 CIL 2020-21 Promotion of horticulture in aspirational district \nSimdega 0.63 Ongoing \n7 ECL 2021-22 \nProviding fund for Development and Repairing \nof basic infrastructure and procurement of \nmedical equipments for the COVID care centers \nat different Hospitals, Health centers & other \nCOVID centers of Deoghar District \n3.00 Ongoing \n8 BCCL 2021-22 \nFinancial assistance through depository mode to \nDhanbad District Administration to combat \nCOVID-19 \n1.00 Fund \ntransferred \n9 CCL 2021-22 Up-gradation of  of 100 Anganwadi Center into \nModel Anganwadi Center at Chatra District 1.50 Ongoing \n10 CCL 2020-21 Transfer of fund to Govt. of Jharkhand for \nCOVID-19 relief 20.00 Completed \n\n11 CCL 2020-21 Establishment of Centralized kitchen for Mid -\nDay Meal Scheme 7.72 Fund \ntransferred \n12 CCL 2020-21 \nUpgradation of Anganwadi  Centres (AWCs) \ninto Model Anganwadi Centres  in Ranchi \nDistrict \n2.25 Fund \ntransferred \n13 CCL 2020-21 \nUpgradation of Anganwadi Centres  (AWCs) \ninto Model Anganwadi Centres \nin Bokaro District  \n1.50 Fund \ntransferred \n14 CCL 2020-21 \nUpgradation of Anganwadi Centres  (AWCs) \ninto Model Anganwadi Centres  at Latehar \nDistrict  \n2.51 Fund \ntransferred \n15 CCL 2020-21 Running and maintenance of sports academy at \nHotwar, Ranchi for FY 20-21 6.48 Completed \n16 CCL 2020-21 1500 Nos. Household Solar light units in \nAmrapali Opencast project villages 1.12 Completed \n17 BCCL 2020-21 \nDepository mode financial assistance to \nDhanbad District Administration for works to be \nundertaken to combat COVID -19 situation in \nDhanbad district \n2.00 Completed \n18 BCCL 2020-21 \nDepository mode funds transfer to Giridih  \nDistrict Administration for development \nactivities to be undertaken in Aspirational \nDistrict Giridih \n1.22 Completed \n19 CCL 2019-20 \n24 Nos. Of Deep bore wells with Solar Powered \nSubmersible pump sets with water storage &  \nwater supply facilities in Project Affected \nvillages of Magadh Amrapali area \n3.04 Completed \n20 CCL 2019-20 Financial Support to State AYUSH Society for \norganizing Yoga Day 1.04 Comple