    "ls|LS17_S6_U_158": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI,\nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *158\nANSWERED ON 29.07.2021\nDAMS AND WATER PROJECTS IN GUJARAT\n*158.       SHRI PATEL HASMUKHBHAI SOMABHAI\nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government has sanctioned a number of dams and water projects in Gujarat during the last\nthree years;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) the details of funds sanctioned for these projects?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF JAL SHAKTI\n(SHRI GAJENDRA SINGH SHEKHAWAT)\n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n******\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED QUESTION\nNO.*158 TO BE ANSWERED ON 29.07.2021 IN LOK SABHA REGARDING “DAMS AND\nWATER PROJECTS IN GUJARAT” RAISED BY SHRI PATEL HASMUKHBHAI SOMABHAI.\n(a) to (c) Water resources projects are planned, funded, executed, and maintained by the State\nGovernments themselves as per their own resources and priorities. Role of Government of India is limited\nto providing technical support and, in some cases, partial financia l assistance under the existing schemes\nbeing implemented by the Ministry of Jal Shakti.\nA cluster of 61 water bodies from Gujarat was included in the year 2018 -19 under Repair,\nRenovation and Restoration (RRR) of Water Bodies scheme of Pradhan Mantri Kr ishi Sinchayee Yojana-\nHar Khet Ko Pani (PMKSY -HKKP). Estimated cost of the scheme is Rs. 102.90 crore, with irrigation\npotential creation target of 11,364 hectare. Central Assistance (CA) of Rs. 8.81 crore has been released to\nthe scheme so far.\nFurther, a project with estimated cost of Rs. 163.29 crore has been sanctioned in 2019 -2020\nunder PMKSY -HKKP Ground Water Development component. The project envisages construction of\n2,512 large diameter dug wells, to create 3,768 hectare of irrigation command a rea by ground water.\nCentral assistance of Rs. 6.0 crore has been released for the project so far.\nFurther, Sardar Sarovar Project was included under Accelerated Irrigation Benefit Programme\n(AIBP) and Command Area Development and Water Management (CADWM ) components of PMKSY in\n2016. The central assistance released by Government of India during the last three years, i.e., from 2018 -\n19 to 2020-21 for the project is Rs.2,057.64 crore.\nAlso, since August 2019, Government of India in partnership with States is implementing Jal\nJeevan Mission (JJM) to make provision of tap water supply in adequate quantity and of prescribed\nquality, on regular and long -term basis through tap water connection to every rural household in the\ncountry by 2024. Since the launch of mission on 15 th August, 2019, an amount of Rs.2,226.04 crore has\nbeen released to Government of Gujarat. 13,45,495 rural households have been provided with tap water\nconnection in the State (as on 23.07.2021).\n*****",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_159": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nLOK SABHA \n    STARRED QUESTION NO. 159 \n    ANSWERED ON 29TH JULY, 2021 \n \nEAST WEST CORRIDOR \n \n*159.   DR. RAJDEEP ROY \n   Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n                  ������  ������������  ����  ��������������  �������� \n be pleased to state: \n(a) the present status of the work on the 25.2 kms stretch of the East -\nWest Corridor between Balacherra and Harangajao in Assam; and  \n(b) the present status of the Multi Modal Logistics Park proposed to \nbe constructed in Silchar? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a)� & (b)   A statement is laid on the table of the House.- \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *159 FOR ANSWER ON 29.07.2021 ASKED BY DR. \nRAJDEEP ROY REGARDING EAST WEST CORRIDOR. \n \n(a)�  The physical progress for the four laning of Balacherra to \nHarangajao section of NH �� 29 (old NH �� 54 ) is 32.98% and the length \ncompleted till date is 10.36 km. \n \n(b)�    Ministry has assigned NHIDCL to carryout the DPR study for MMLP \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\nhas been awarded to Consortium of M/s Ta ta Consulting Engineers Ltd. (TCE)  \nand M/s CBRE South Asia Private Limited.  The DPR work has commenced on \n09.04.2021 for the site (45.3 acres) proposed by Govt of Assam vide letter \ndated 01.04.2021.   \n \n***** \n \n�",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_16": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 16 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n \nTechnical Education Quality Improvement Programme \n \n*16. SHRIMATI RAKSHA NIKHIL KHADSE: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is making continuous efforts to convince the Focused \nState Governments to prepare a sustainability plan for the Technical Education \nQuality Improvement Programme (TEQIP-III) of the Government to continue \nthe services rendered by the faculties engaged to upgrade the engineering \neducation in the focused States; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(c)  the steps taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to safeguard this \ntechnical force engaged under TEQIP-III for which the programme period has \nended in March, 2021? \n \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n(a) to (c): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (c) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 16 FOR 19.07.2021 ASKED BY \nSHRIMATI RAKSHA NIKHIL KHADSE, HON’BLE MEMBER OF \nPARLIAMENT REGARDING TECHNICAL EDUCATION QUALITY \nIMPROVEMENT PROGRAMME. \n \n(a to b) The Government of India has been making continuous efforts to ensure that \nthe focus State Governments prepare a sustainability plan for the Technical  \nEducation Quality Improvement Programme (TEQIP-III). Several communications \nhave been sent to the focus States requesting for preparation of a sustainability plan \nfor filling up vacant faculty positions through regular recruitments so as to avoid any \nacademic standstill beyond the project period i.e 30th September 2021. \n Ministry of Education has also written to the Chief Secretaries of Focus \nStates requesting to plan for continuation of activities undertaken during TEQIP-III, \nfor maintaining the quality of technical education. \n(c) Government of India has extended the TEQIP III project including the tenure \nof the temporary project faculties once from 30th September 2020 to 31st March 2021 \nand then finally up to 30th September 2021. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_160": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 160 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n \nResults of Board Exams \n \n160.  SHRI D.M. KATHIR ANAND: \nSHRI GAURAV GOGOI:  \nSHRI MANICKAM TAGORE B.:  \nSHRI KULDEEP RAI SHARMA:  \nSHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE:  \nDR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE: \nDR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR. S.:  \nSHRI THIRUNAVUKKARASAR SU:  \nSHRI SUNIL DATTATRAY TATKARE:  \nDR. AMOL RAMSING KOLHE: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the C BSE cancelled class X and XII Board Exams 2021 due to pandemic \nsituation in the country and if so, the criteria adopted by the CBSE to determine the 12th \nclass result;  \n \n(b) whether the Government is aware that there is widespread discontentment among the \nstudents across the country about the CBSE evaluation criteria and if so, the steps \ntaken/propose to be taken by the Government; \n \n(c) whether the Government has taken into account the challenges faced by the students of \nclass 12 during academic year 2020-2021 and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(d) whether the average scores of students of class 12 in pre -board examination in many \nschools were lower than the previous years average and if so, the details thereof and the \nreasons therefor;  \n \n(e) whether the CBSE proposes to take into account the above facts while preparing class 12 \nresults; \n \n(f) whether only around 50 percent of the students had online connections for class 12 as \nresult of which online education could not reach all students affecting them adverse ly; \nand  \n\n(g) if so, whether the Government proposes to provide required infrastructure for online \neducation to students who are promoted to class 12? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a): Yes Sir. The annual examinations for classe s X and XII have been cancelled by the \nBoard.  Following criteria has been adopted by Central Board of Secondary Education \n(CBSE) to prepare the results of Class-XII:-  \n \n(i) The assessment of theory portion will be done by the school based on the following: \n \nClass XII Marks based on Unit Test/Mid-Term/ Pre-Board Exam 40 % \nClass XI Marks based on theory component of final exam 30 % \nClass X Marks based on average theory component of best three \nperforming subjects out of main 5 subjects. \n30 % \n \n(ii) The mark s of Practical / Internal Assessment etc. of class – XII will be on actual \nbasis as uploaded by the school on the CBSE portal. \n \n(b): Policy for preparation of results has been approved by the Hon’ble Supreme Court of \nIndia in the matter of Mamta Sharma Vs CBSE. \n \n(c) and (e): Following challenges were observed and addressed:- \n \n• Diversity in instructional methods, \n• Non-uniform evaluation process, \n• Multiplicity in types of assessment conducted by the schools and  \n• Conduct of online and offline classes.  \n  \n(d): The conduct of pre-board examination is the prerogative of individual schools.  No data \nof the conduct of pre-board examinations is collected by CBSE. \n \n(f) and (g): Online classes are being conducted at the schools by employing various digital tools \nin the fo rm of DIKSHA portal ( https://diksha.gov.in/), SWAYAM Portal \n(swayam.gov.in), SWAYAM Prabha, DD Channel, e -Pathshala \n(https://epathshala.nit.in/), NROER (National Repository o f Open Educational \nResources) portal (https://nroer.gov.in/welcome). \n  \nLearning programmes have also been started in the form of offline learning tools in \nthe form of alternative academic calendar by NCERT radio, community radio and \nCBSE podcasts, toll free numbers, missed call, SMS based requests for audio \ncontent, localized radio content for edutainment etc.  The medium of TV, radio  and \ntextbooks is also used for the students who do not have digital means. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_161": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.161 \nANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF RAMAYANA CIRCUIT \n \n161.  SHRI SANGAM LAL GUPTA:  \nSHRI MANOJ TIWARI:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Go vernment has any proposal to develop \nRamayana Circuit in the near future;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor;  \n(d)  whether any other religions circuit is also under consideration; \nand  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF TOURISM            (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n(a) to (e): Ramayana Circuit is one of the identified thematic circuit \nof ‘Swadesh Darshan’ scheme of the Ministry of Tourism under \nwhich 2 projects have been sanctioned. The Ministry has also \nsanctioned projects under Buddhist, Tirthankar, Krishna and \nSpiritual Circuits.  \n \nIn addition, the Ministry of Tourism  provides  financial  \nassistance  to  State Governments / Union Territory  Administrations \nfor  integrated  development of  identified  pilgri mage and  heritage  \ndestinations  under  ‘National Mission on  Pilgrimage Rejuvenation \nand  Spiritual, Heritage Augmentation Drive (PRASHAD)’  scheme.  \n \nThe detail of projects sanctioned under Ramayana, Krishna,  \nSpiritual, Tirthankar and Buddhist Circuits  under  Swadesh Darshan  \nscheme  and  the  detail of  the  projects  sanctioned under  \n‘PRASHAD’  scheme is  annexed.     \n*******\n\n             ANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF L OK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 161 ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \nDEVELOPMENT OF RAMAYANA CIRCUIT. \n \nTHE DETAIL OF PROJECTS SANCTIONED UNDER RAMAYANA, \nBUDDHIST, TIRTHANKAR, KRISHNA AND SPIRITUAL CIRCUITS OF \nSWADESH DARSHAN SCHEME AND DETAIL OF PROJECTS \nSANCTIONED UNDER PRASHAD SCHEME.   \n       (Amt. in Rs. crore) \nS.  \nNo. \nName of \nState \nName of \nCircuit & \nYear \nProject Name Amt. \nSancti