    "ls|LS17_S6_U_3": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 3 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19TH July, 2021 \n \nIncreasing Prices of Petroleum Products \n \n*3. SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n      SHRI K. MURALEEDHARAN: \n \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम और \u0000ाकृ\u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ी   \n \n Will the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether  it  has  come  to  the  notice  of  the Government  that  the  prices  of  petrol  and  \ndiesel  are increasing; \n \n(b) if so, the action taken to make available petrol and diesel at reasonable prices; \n \n(c) whether  it  has  come  to  the  notice  of  the Government  that  the  duties  and  taxes  on  \npetrol  and diesel are more than the cost thereof and if so, the action taken  thereon; \n \n(d) the details of the number of times the Government has  increased  the  prices  of  \npetroleum  products  like diesel, petrol and domestic LPG cylinder during the last six \nmonths; and \n \n(e) whether the Government has taken any steps to reduce the prices of petroleum products \nand if so, the details thereof? \n \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkÑfrd xSl; ea=h \n (\u0000ी हरद\u0000प \u0000संह पु\u0000र) \nMINISTER OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n(SHRIHARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 3 asked \nby Shri N.K. Premachandran and Shri K. Muraleedharan to be answered on 19 th July, \n2021 regarding “Increasing Prices of Petroleum Products”. \n \n \n(a) & (b):   Prices of petrol and diesel are market-determined with effect from 26.06.2010 and \n19.10.2014 respectively. Since then, the Public Sector Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs) have \nbeen taking appropriate decision on pricing of petrol and diesel on the basis of international \nproduct prices and other market conditions. . The OMCs have increased and decreased the prices \nof petrol and diesel according to changes in international prices and rupee dollar exchange \nrate.      \n \n(c):  The price break up of Petrol and Diesel at Delhi as on 15th July 2021 is as under: \nParticulars Unit Petrol Diesel \nBase Price (including Dealers commission) Rs/Ltr 44.94 44.80 \nAdd :  Excise Duty (levied by the Centre Govt.) Rs/Ltr 32.90 31.80 \nAdd : VAT (including VAT on Dealer Commission) \n(levied by the State Govt.) Rs/Ltr 23.35 13.12 \nRetail Selling Price at Delhi          Rs/Ltr 101.19 89.72 \n \n(d): The details of the number of times the prices of petrol, diesel and LPG has changed at Delhi \nsince 1st January, 2021 till 09th July, 2021 by OMCs are as under: \n \n Petrol Diesel Domestic \nLPG \nIncrease 63 61 5 \nDecrease 4 4 1 \nNo Change 123 125 - \n \n(e): The prices of petroleum products are linked to the price of respective products in the \ninternational market.  Oil Marketing Companies take a decision on retail selling price based  on \nvarious factors including international product prices, exchange rate, tax structure, inland freight \nand other cost elements.  \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_30": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK  SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 30 \n  ANSWERED ON 20/07/2021 \nPMGSY IN UTTAR PRADESH \n \n*30.  SHRI LALLU SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of the allotted proposals and fund s allocated district-wise in Uttar Pradesh \nunder the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana Phase-III; \n(b)  the present status of allotted proposals under  the said scheme; \n(c)  whether the projects approved for Uttar Prades h are likely to be completed within the \nstipulated time; and \n(d)  if not, the details thereof and the reasons th erefor?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n(a) to (d):    A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.30 \ndue for answer on 20.07.2021 \n \n(a)&(b)  The Government approved PMGSY-III in July,  2019 for consolidation of 1,25,000 Km \nof Through Routes and Major Rural Links connecting habitations, inter-alia, to Gramin \nAgricultural Markets (GrAMs), Higher Secondary Scho ols and Hospitals. The period of \nimplementation of PMGSY-III is upto March, 2025. Th e target road length for the State of Uttar \nPradesh under PMGSY-III is 18,937.5 km. So far proposal for a length of 6287.37 km (898 roads \nand 5 long span bridges) with a total cost of Rs 4, 177.80 crore (Central Share Rs 2,506.33 crore \nand State Share Rs 1,671.47 crore) has been sanctio ned to the State of Uttar Pradesh, out of \nwhich 31.94 km of road length has been completed ti ll 15 \nth  July, 2021. District-wise details of \nsanctioned works to the State of Uttar Pradesh and their present status are given at Annexure .  \n \n The funds for implementation of the PMGSY are rele ased by the Ministry to the States/ \nUTs as a whole, considering unspent balances of pre vious releases available with the State and \nthe pace of expenditure. As on 1 \nst  April, 2021, unspent balance available with the St ate of Uttar \nPradesh was Rs 284.11 crore, out of which an expend iture of Rs 171.14 crore has been incurred \ntill 15 th  July, 2021. The balance fund available with the St ate as on 15 th  July, 2021 is Rs 112.97 \ncrore. The State has not yet demanded any programme  fund during the current financial year \n2021-22. \n \n(c)& (d) As per the programme guidelines, the relevant road projects should be completed within \na period of 12 working months from the date of issu e of the work order. In this connection it has \nbeen further clarified in the programme guidelines that: where a package comprises more than \none roadwork, the total time given for completion o f the package shall not exceed 18 calendar \nmonths. Similarly, time period of 21-24 months woul d be allowed for completion of cross \ndrainage works exceeding 25-meter in length, depending on site conditions.   \n   \n****** \n\nAnnexure \nAnnexure referred to Lok Sabha Starred Question No 30 to answered on 20.7.2021 \nSr.No. District Name No of \nRoad \nworks \nSanctioned \nRoad \nLength \nSanctioned \n \n(km) \nNo of \nBridge \nWorks \nSanctioned \n \nNo of \nRoad \nWorks \nCompleted \nNo of \nBridge \nWorks \nCompleted \nRoad \nLength \nCompleted \n \n(km) \nBalanced \nRoad \nLength \n(km) \n1 Agra 4  25.750  0 0 0 8.300  17.450  \n2 Aligarh 13  132.700  0 0 0 0.000  132.700  \n3 Prayagraj 25  176.300  0 0 0 0.000  176.300  \n4 Ambedkarnagar 17  121.600  0 0 0 0.000  121.600  \n5 Auraiya 4  27.650  0 0 0 0.000  27.650  \n6 Azamgarh 24  146.800  0 0 0 5.740  141.060  \n7 Badaun 13  88.455  0 0 0 0.000  88.455  \n8 Baghpat 10  62.415  0 0 0 0.000  62.415  \n9 Bahraich 11  94.560  0 0 0 0.000  94.560  \n10 Ballia 21  154.325  0 0 0 0.000  154.325  \n11 Balrampur 7  45.350  0 0 0 6.400  38.950  \n12 Banda 3  18.400  0 0 0 0.000  18.400  \n13 Barabanki 13  80.310  0 0 0 0.000  80.310  \