    "ls|LS17_S6_U_85": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE  \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.85 \nANSWERED ON 26.7.2021 \n \n \nREVENUE LOSS DURING LOCKDOWN \n \n \n*85 SHRI BHAGWANT MANN: \nSHRI VIJYAKUMAR (ALIAS) VIJYA VASANTH: \n  \n \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the UNESCO world heritage sites and ASI protected monuments were \nclosed for a number of days with the imposing of lockdown 2.0 in various parts of \nthe country due to Covid-19 situation; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the amount of revenue loss incurred as a result thereof; \n(d) whether any steps have been taken to improve the facilities for the visiting public \nin the heritage sites/monuments to increase the footfall, if so, the details thereof, \nmonument-wise and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(e) whether the Government has increased the daily entry limit/ticket sales in the \nmonuments; and \n(f) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF CULTURE, TOURISM AND DEVELOPMENT OF \nNORTH EASTERN REGION \n               \n(SHRI G.KISHAN REDDY) \n \n \n \n(a) to (f)  A statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (f) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 85 FOR 26.07.2021 \n \n \n(a)&(b) The Centrally protected monuments including Centrally protected World \nHeritage Sites were closed for a period of 61 days (from 16.4.2021 to  \n15.6.2021) during lockdown 2.0 in view of Covid-19 situation.  \n \n(c) The estimated loss of revenue due to closing of ticketed monuments in view of \nimposing of lockdown 2.0 (Covid -19 situation) is Approx. Rs.35.40 crores, the \ncalculation is based on revenue lost due to lack of sales of tickets. \n \n(d) Providing basic facilities/amenities like drinking water, toilets, facilities for \nphysically challenged, pathways, signage, vehicle parking, cloak rooms, etc.  at \ncentrally protected monuments/sites including improvement threof is a regular \nphenomenon, which Archaeol ogical Survey of India(ASI)  undertakes, as per \nrequirements.  Such fac ilities are available at ASI’s World Heritage Sites, \ncentrally protected ticketed monuments and other monuments visited by \ntourists.  \nThe monume nt-wise details are available at https://asi.nic.in/facilities-at-\nmonument/ \n \n(e)&(f) \n \n \nThere is no limit on entry of visitors/ticket sales imposed during lockdown 2.0.   \nWhere ever the monuments are located SoP  of concerned State Government \nare followed.  \n \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_86": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF REVENUE \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 86 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, JULY 19, 2021/ASHADHA 28, 1943 (SAKA) \n \nSETTING UP OF AARS \n \n86. SHRI SUSHIL KUMAR SINGH: \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a)whether it is a fact that in-principle approval was given to the setting up of national benches of \nAuthority on Advanced rulings (AARs) and Appellate Authority of Advanced Rulings (AAR) in \nthe 31st meeting of GST council held on 22nd December 2018,;  \n(b) if so, whether such benches at national level and regional benches of AAR have been set up;  \n(c) if so, the details of such benches;  \n(d) if not, the reasons for delay in setting up such benches and the proposed timeline to set up \nthem; and  \n(e) the comprehensive list of contradictory AAR rulings? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FINANCE (SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) The GST Council in its 31st Meeting held on 22nd  December 2018  gave in -principle \napproval for setting up of an appellate body at National level, where there are conflicting \ndecisions of two or more different Appellate Authorities for Advance Ruling (AAAR) on the \nsame issue in respect of a taxpayer having the same Permanent Account Number (PAN) and \nregistered in two or more States. \n(b) to (d) Authorities for Advance Ruling (AAR) and Appellate Authorities for Advance Ruling \n(AAAR) have already been set up in all the States and Union territories under their respective \nSGST / UTGST Acts.  \nAs regards setting up of National Appellate Authority for Advance Ruling, the relevant \nprovision under the CGST Act, 2017 was introduced through the Finance (No. 2) Act, 2019. \nHowever, the same would be notified on a date to be recommended the GST Council. The \nNational Appellate Authority for Advance Ruling can be constituted only after the said provision \nis notified.  \n \n(e) The rulings given by AAR and AAAR depend upon the specific facts in respect of a \nparticular taxpayer who seeks a ruling and are not generic to an issue.  \nAs such, no details of co ntradictory rulings in cases where facts are similar, are \nmaintained. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S6_U_87": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 87 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2021 \n  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT CENTRES IN NORTH EASTERN REGION \n \n† 87.   SHRI DILIP SAIKIA:  \n  \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n  \n(a)  the number of proposals for opening of skill d evelopment centres received by \nthe Government from the North-Eastern States includ ing Assam during the last two \nyears; \n \n(b)  if so, the number of such proposal accepted du ring the current financial year \nalong with the funds relased thereof; and \n \n(c)  the details of the proposals received from Ass am, district-wise? \n \nANSWER  \n \nTHE MINISTER OF \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (c) Ministry of Skill Development and Entrep reneurship (MSDE) promotes \nestablishment of model and aspirational skill devel opment centres known as Pradhan \nMantri Kaushal Kendras (PMKK) in every district of the country. During the last two \nfinancial years (2019 – 20 and 2020-21), 123 propos als were received out of which 30 \nproposals were accepted from North East states of I ndia. Since the concerned PMKKs \nwere self-funded, no funds were released from MSDE in the North East States of India \nduring the last two financial years (2019 -20, 2020 -21). No proposals were received \nfrom the State of Assam during the last two financial years. \n \n****** \n \n \n ",
